    {
      "sections": [
        {
          "kind": "intro",
          "paragraphs": [
            "Austrian main signals say whether and how fast you may pass (**Halt**, **Frei**, **Frei mit 40**, **Frei mit 60**); distant signals (**Vorsignale**) what the next main signal shows. Other speeds come from speed indicators beside the signal. On the **Semmeringbahn** (1116, 4024) **PZB 90** watches the signals; on the **Mittenwaldbahn** (1020, 1989) it is the older **Indusi I60**, and the German section to the border has German signals (see the Germany manual). Speeds in km/h. Quadrant controls are from TheJAG's ÖBB profiles: the same layout as the German trains."
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "systems",
          "title": "Safety systems",
          "cols": 4,
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "PZB 90",
              "full": "Punktförmige Zugbeeinflussung",
              "summary": "Magnets at **1000 Hz** (distant signal), **500 Hz** (before some main signals; rare in Austria) and **2000 Hz** (main signal). Acknowledge, then keep within the speed curve.",
              "where": "Semmeringbahn: 1116, 4024",
              "quadrant": "**ENG 2** Wachsam, **ENG 1** Frei, **round aux** Befehl 40; right aux square PZB on / off"
            },
            {
              "name": "Indusi I60",
              "full": "Induktive Zugsicherung (1989)",
              "summary": "After **Wachsam** (4 s) be at or below 95 (O) / 75 (M) km/h within **34 s**: one check, no curve. 500 Hz: a spot check at 40. **Frei only releases a penalty brake.**",
              "where": "Mittenwaldbahn: 1020",
              "quadrant": "Same buttons: ENG 2 Wachsam, ENG 1 Frei, round aux Befehl; right aux Indusi"
            },
            {
              "name": "SiFa",
              "full": "Sicherheitsfahrschaltung",
              "summary": "1116 / 4024: after 30 s a lamp, 2.5 s later a buzzer, 2.5 s later the emergency brake. **1020: no lamp**: a buzzer after 30 s, an alarm 75 m later, the brake 75 m after that.",
              "where": "Every ÖBB train",
              "quadrant": "**Gear lever** = SiFa reset; left aux square SiFa on / off"
            },
            {
              "name": "LZB / ETCS",
              "full": "Continuous systems",
              "summary": "LZB on parts of the Westbahn and ETCS on new lines in the real world; neither on these TSW routes.",
              "where": "–",
              "quadrant": ""
            }
          ]
        },
